From cb1a4062f644da15c2fa7715ecf0b0c8325415e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chatwithgod <283797944+chatwithgod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:19:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: let trusted code execute bounded Responses rounds

Offer one compiled executor after the gateway has selected and signed a native
streaming Responses request. It retains the selected identity, model and transport,
closes each reply before calling again and is limited to eight upstream calls.
Failure and panic do not automatically replay the initial request. With no
executor, forwarding is unchanged. Valid folded billing totals remain distinct
from visible context usage. This is trusted in-process code, not a JS sandbox.

Reapplied the independently extracted host patch to the observed upstream head
bca0d6d69a806ae941bf9a5a6fafe4c7e03322b9, 210 commits after the prior pinned
ffa07395 base. No runtime changes beyond the already published extension.
The Reflow bridge, its dependency and its test-only fixes are separate.

Verification on Windows with original module files, nogui, package and test
parallelism 1: ordinary and race each 10 pass / 0 skip / 0 fail. The five
selected top-level tests cover native gateway wiring, translated-route bypass,
folded usage, registration, cancellation and call bounds. Disabling the registered
executor makes TestExecutionExtensionThroughNativeCodexGateway fail behaviorally:
HTTP 200, one upstream request instead of two. Source was restored before race.
Temporary homes removed, module locks unchanged, gofmt -l printed nothing.
Raw output bodies were not saved; diagnostics contain numbers and test events.

Not run at this head: full host suite, whole-host build/vet matrix, GUI, native
Linux/macOS execution or real accounts. This is a discussion candidate, not a
merge or release acceptance. No upstream issue/PR or remote push was performed.
