index 87fbb9b3f985777841884d892250d7fc88e31a15..428eb07bfac736b3e4a8b6e3873d4ce2b7e226d7 100644
--- a/docs/subsystems/gateway-middleware.md
+++ b/docs/subsystems/gateway-middleware.md
@@ -21,6 +21,12 @@ plugins.json is the source of truth for which middleware is installed and on, in
 
 ## Runtime path
 
+### Optional Responses execution
+
+The compiled execution extension in [`internal/gwexec`](../../internal/gwexec/gwexec.go) is separate from the JavaScript and Bun hooks. [`executeResponses`](../../internal/gateway/execution.go) offers it only native Codex passthrough and streaming Responses-to-Responses requests, after normal preparation and signing. Translations, non-streaming requests, compaction and other APIs bypass it. The callback retains the selected endpoint, account, model, context and transport limits; it exposes the body and an opaque account-and-endpoint scope, not credentials. This is an interface for trusted in-process code, not a plugin sandbox.
+
+Only the last registered executor runs. Each request permits at most eight upstream calls including the first, and requires the preceding response to be closed before another call. An extension error or panic returns an error without automatically replaying the original request. Existing gateway error handling and candidate fallback remain outside this interface. A folded Responses reply may carry `metadata.proxy_billed_usage` and `proxy_rounds`: the passthrough usage reader accepts valid totals that do not reduce any ordinary usage component, while leaving the client stream unchanged ([`execution_usage.go`](../../internal/gateway/execution_usage.go)).
+
 1. `serveAgent` establishes the [gateway session identity and optional recording](gateway-sessions.md), runs any [asynchronous request hooks](gateway-request-hooks.md) through Bun, then calls `Begin` on each registered `gwmw.Agent` (the JS chain's is `middleware.Begin`) with the request's protocol, model, stream flag, path and agent. With no middleware it calls `serve` directly.
 2. `Run.Request` passes the agent's body, in its own API, to each `onRequest` in turn. An object returned is the body the next middleware and the gateway get; `undefined` keeps the bytes as they were. `ctx.reject(status, message)` stops the chain, and the agent gets that error in its API's shape (`writeError`).
 3. `Run.Tried` runs each `onProvider` on the body each time `serve` tries it on a provider, just before that try is sent (`triedOn` in the candidate loop of `gateway.go`; `serveAgent` puts the runs that are `gwmw.Tried` on the request's context). `ctx.provider` says which: `id`, `name`, `account` (the subscription's kind, as `accountAgent` gives it: `claude`, `antigravity`, …; absent for a key) and `model`, the model's id there. Every try starts again from the body `onRequest` left, so what one provider is sent changes no other try's: this is how a plugin acts on one vendor only, for an agent such as Claude Desktop whose model names say nothing of where they go. `null` and `ctx.reject` turn nothing away here; the request has been routed.
